"No free lunch, entropy"
Local entropy tax exists; globally the vacuum can book it as 
potential, which is why Guth called the universe the ultimate 
free lunch.

Every projection has a discard cost, but in an emergent 
system that cost returns to potential. Vacuum absorbs the 
discard, so the universe can be a free lunch (Guth).

TYPES
S     entropy (disorder / unavailable energy)
E+    positive energy (matter, radiation, vacuum energy)
E-    negative gravitational potential energy
V     vacuum / inflaton potential
P     projection (local realization of a state)

VARIABLES / RELATIONS
dS/dt  >= 0          local entropy production (2nd law)
E_tot  = E+ + E-  ~ 0   closed FLRW / inflationary universe
Delta E_discard -> V    cost recycled into potential, not lost
inflation: V drives exponential expansion, then decays to radiation

FUNDAMENTALS
No-free-lunch (colloquial): you cannot create usable order 
without paying entropy or energy elsewhere.

Thermodynamic: heat engines and computation have irreducible 
waste heat.

Cosmological exception (Guth): total energy of a spatially flat
universe can be zero. Positive energy of stuff is canceled by 
negative gravitational binding. Vacuum energy can source expansion 
without a net energy input from "outside."

Emergent-system reading: local projections (galaxies, observers, 
computations) still pay discard costs, but those costs are absorbed 
by the larger vacuum/potential so the global ledger stays balanced.
